From 89b5371311e3924c84de0fc85e0a50bb14231c45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:31:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] fix(a2ui): name an action by the control pressed, never
 its producer id
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a person used an agent's surface, the lifecycle line read
"earthscope.stations.selected recorded" (live 2026-11-18): only the two built-in
actions had words, and any other action printed its producer identifier, which
the repository's rules keep out of primary copy. The line now names the control
the person pressed, from the lifecycle's source_component_id and that control's
literal label (or its child's), as "“Analyse selected station” recorded", and
falls back to "Your choice". A bound label is not read. The line also loses its
extra divider.

The existing lifecycle tests pinned the raw action name in the visible text;
they now assert it is never shown. The component-map reader moves to
lib/a2ui/surface-components.ts, which question-navigation now shares.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BHQAws7LSR8fWEJvjbJM4q
